From ef50ecce514f06babfc873f83c4c287bf706aed2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:47:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] ci: run a single Python 3.14 lane

The test and timing-sensitive matrices, the landscape long-run proofs and
every container job move to the digest-pinned python:3.14-bookworm
image; the 3.12 lane and its evidence downloads and validation step are
gone, and the 3.14 lane is the coverage lane. The live-provider, mutation
and judge-gate workflows use 3.14 too. actionlint 1.7.12 (the pinned,
checksum-verified release) is clean.

scripts/ci_test_shards.py names its lanes once: COVERAGE_PYTHON_VERSION
and SUPPORTED_PYTHON_VERSIONS (3.14 only) replace the 3.12/3.13
literals. The cicd tests now build 3.14 evidence; the negative controls
use an unsupported version (3.13), new ones refuse every non-3.14 lane,
and re-admitting 3.13 in the script turns them red. Cases that existed
only for the 3.12 non-coverage lane are removed. The "Run tests without
coverage" steps can no longer run but are kept, as the activation
contract still pins them.

Required status-check contexts change with the job names, e.g.
"Test (Python 3.14, shard N)" and "Timing-sensitive tests (Python 3.14)";
the repository ruleset must be updated to match before this can merge.

